 ",[214,532,254],{}," at runtime only and never writes it to the Wolf config.",[227,535,537],{"id":536},"what-wolf-does-on-a-pilot-bench","What Wolf does on a Pilot bench",[539,540,541,557],"table",{},[542,543,544],"thead",{},[545,546,547,551,554],"tr",{},[548,549,550],"th",{},"Area",[548,552,553],{},"What Wolf does",[548,555,556],{},"Status",[558,559,560,582,604,625,642,667,685,706,735,748],"tbody",{},[545,561,562,566,579],{},[563,564,565],"td",{},"Discovery",[563,567,568,569,571,572,255,574,259,576,578],{},"Searches ",[214,570,250],{}," in addition to the old globs. A ",[214,573,254],{},[214,575,258],{},[214,577,262],{}," is treated as a Pilot bench and read with its real keys",[563,580,581],{},"done, unit tested",[545,583,584,587,602],{},[563,585,586],{},"Sites",[563,588,589,590,593,594,597,598,601],{},"Reads ",[214,591,592],{},"sites\u002F*\u002Fsite_config.json",", plus ",[214,595,596],{},"domains"," (plain strings or ",[214,599,600],{},"{\"domain\": …, \"route\": …}",") for host → site mapping",[563,603,581],{},[545,605,606,609,623],{},[563,607,608],{},"Process logs",[563,610,611,612,615,616,615,619,622],{},"Tails ",[214,613,614],{},"web",", ",[214,617,618],{},"schedule",[214,620,621],{},"worker_\u003Cqueues>_\u003Ci>"," and their stderr files, for both the systemd and the supervisor naming",[563,624,581],{},[545,626,627,630,640],{},[563,628,629],{},"nginx",[563,631,611,632,635,636,639],{},[214,633,634],{},"\u003Cbench>\u002Flogs\u002Fnginx-access.log",", in the ",[214,637,638],{},"pilot_access"," format",[563,641,581],{},[545,643,644,647,664],{},[563,645,646],{},"Redis queue",[563,648,589,649,652,653,656,657,333,660,663],{},[214,650,651],{},"queue_length",", the RQ failed\u002Fstarted registries, live workers and Redis memory\u002Fevictions from ",[214,654,655],{},"redis:\u002F\u002F127.0.0.1:\u003C[redis] queue_port>",". ",[214,658,659],{},"redis_queue",[214,661,662],{},"common_site_config.json"," takes precedence when present",[563,665,666],{},"done",[545,668,669,672,682],{},[563,670,671],{},"Backups, TLS, MariaDB",[563,673,674,675,678,679,681],{},"Same as on any bench: ",[214,676,677],{},"sites\u002F\u003Csite>\u002Fprivate\u002Fbackups\u002F",", each site and ",[214,680,596],{}," entry, the site's database credentials",[563,683,684],{},"done (generic)",[545,686,687,690,703],{},[563,688,689],{},"Processes",[563,691,692,695,696,699,700,702],{},[214,693,694],{},"supervisorctl status",", else systemd units whose name contains the bench name (",[214,697,698],{},"bench_processes_down","). If Pilot's unit or program names do not contain the ",[214,701,258],{},", nothing is reported",[563,704,705],{},"unverified",[545,707,708,711,733],{},[563,709,710],{},"Deployments",[563,712,713,714,717,718,720,721,724,725,728,729,732],{},"A ",[214,715,716],{},"deployment"," event (category ",[214,719,344],{},") when an update, migrate, branch switch, app install, build, restart or restore task ",[209,722,723],{},"starts",", and an ",[214,726,727],{},"error"," event (",[214,730,731],{},"pilot_task_failed",") when one fails. Read from the Admin API, or from the task files",[563,734,581],{},[545,736,737,740,743],{},[563,738,739],{},"\"Enable Wolf for this bench\" toggle in Pilot",[563,741,742],{},"Needs a change in frappe\u002Fpilot",[563,744,745],{},[209,746,747],{},"not done",[545,749,750,753,758],{},[563,751,752],{},"Real Pilot host",[563,754,755],{},[209,756,757],{},"Not tested yet",[563,759,760],{},"—",[198,762,763,764,225],{},"The metrics themselves are described on ",[201,765,60],{"href":61},[227,767,769],{"id":768},"bench-layout","Bench layout",[241,771,773],{"id":772},"benches","Benches",[198,775,776,777,780,781,784,785,788,789,791],{},"Pilot's ",[214,778,779],{},"install.sh"," installs into ",[214,782,783],{},"$HOME\u002Fpilot",". Benches live in ",[214,786,787],{},"~\u002Fpilot\u002Fbenches\u002F\u003Cname>\u002F"," by default. On a root-only VPS, the installer creates a non-root bench user, hence the ",[214,790,250],{}," glob.",[198,793,794,795,615,798,615,801,615,804,615,807,615,810,259,813,225],{},"Each bench holds ",[214,796,797],{},"apps\u002F",[214,799,800],{},"sites\u002F",[214,802,803],{},"env\u002F",[214,805,806],{},"logs\u002F",[214,808,809],{},"config\u002F",[214,811,812],{},"pids\u002F",[214,814,254],{},[241,816,254],{"id":817},"benchtoml",[198,819,820],{},"Wolf reads these keys:",[539,822,823,833],{},[542,824,825],{},[545,826,827,830],{},[548,828,829],{},"Key",[548,831,832],{},"Use",[558,834,835,847,860,877,886],{},[545,836,837,841],{},[563,838,839],{},[214,840,258],{},[563,842,843,844,846],{},"Required, together with ",[214,845,262],{},". The bench name and the Pilot marker",[545,848,849,854],{},[563,850,851],{},[214,852,853],{},"[redis] queue_port",[563,855,856,857],{},"Queue Redis port. Default ",[214,858,859],{},"11000",[545,861,862,867],{},[563,863,864],{},[214,865,866],{},"[admin] port",[563,868,869,870,873,874],{},"Default ",[214,871,872],{},"7000",". The Admin backend binds ",[214,875,876],{},"127.0.0.1:\u003Cport + 1>",[545,878,879,883],{},[563,880,881],{},[214,882,496],{},[563,884,885],{},"Read at runtime only, never written to the Wolf config",[545,887,888,893],{},[563,889,890],{},[214,891,892],{},"[production] enabled",[563,894,895],{},"Kept for information",[198,897,898,900,901,904,905,908,909,912,913,915,916,919],{},[214,899,254],{}," has ",[209,902,903],{},"no"," nginx or logs keys: \"Nginx uses compiled-in defaults; it has no ",[214,906,907],{},"[nginx]"," table\". ",[214,910,911],{},"[monitor]"," only names Pilot's own metric log. A ",[214,914,254],{}," that is not Pilot's (no ",[214,917,918],{},"[bench] python",") still goes through the old defensive parser.",[241,921,608],{"id":922},"process-logs",[198,924,925,926,349],{},"Process logs go to ",[214,927,928],{},"\u003Cbench>\u002Flogs\u002F",[930,931,932,938,947],"ul",{},[933,934,935],"li",{},[214,936,937],{},"web.log",[933,939,940,943,944,225],{},[214,941,942],{},"worker_\u003Cqueue-slug>_\u003Ci>.log",". The slug is the queue list with every non-alphanumeric run replaced by ",[214,945,946],{},"_",[933,948,949],{},[214,950,951],{},"schedule.log",[198,953,954,955,958,959,962,963,966],{},"stderr goes to ",[214,956,957],{},"\u003Clog>.error.log"," under systemd (for example ",[214,960,961],{},"web.log.error.log",") and to ",[214,964,965],{},"\u003Cname>.error.log"," under supervisor. Wolf tails both spellings. Missing files cost nothing.",[198,968,969,970,615,973,259,976,979],{},"Frappe's own ",[214,971,972],{},"frappe.web.log",[214,974,975],{},"scheduler.log",[214,977,978],{},"worker.log"," are tailed as on every bench.",[241,981,629],{"id":629},[198,983,984,985,988,989,991],{},"Each site vhost logs ",[214,986,987],{},"location \u002F"," to ",[214,990,634],{}," in this format:",[269,993,996],{"className":994,"code":995,"language":629,"meta":274,"style":274},"language-nginx shiki shiki-themes material-theme-lighter material-theme material-theme-palenight","log_format pilot_access '$pilot_client_addr [$time_local] \"$request_method $uri\" $status \"$host\" $request_time';\n",[214,997,998],{"__ignoreMap":274},[278,999,1000,1003,1007,1010,1013,1016,1019,1021,1024,1027,1029,1032,1035,1038,1041,1043,1046,1049,1051,1054,1056,1058,1061,1063],{"class":280,"line":281},[278,1001,1002],{"class":362},"log_format ",[278,1004,1006],{"class":1005},"sTEyZ","pilot_access ",[278,1008,1009],{"class":288},"'",[278,1011,1012],{"class":362},"$",[278,1014,1015],{"class":1005},"pilot_client_addr",[278,1017,1018],{"class":288}," [",[278,1020,1012],{"class":362},[278,1022,1023],{"class":1005},"time_local",[278,1025,1026],{"class":288},"] \"",[278,1028,1012],{"class":362},[278,1030,1031],{"class":1005},"request_method",[278,1033,1034],{"class":362}," $",[278,1036,1037],{"class":1005},"uri",[278,1039,1040],{"class":288},"\" ",[278,1042,1012],{"class":362},[278,1044,1045],{"class":1005},"status",[278,1047,1048],{"class":288}," \"",[278,1050,1012],{"class":362},[278,1052,1053],{"class":1005},"host",[278,1055,1040],{"class":288},[278,1057,1012],{"class":362},[278,1059,1060],{"class":1005},"request_time",[278,1062,1009],{"class":288},[278,1064,1065],{"class":362},";\n",[198,1067,1068,1069,1072,1073,225],{},"This is not the combined format: it has no ident or user, no byte count and no protocol. Wolf's nginx parser accepts it. Pilot's own access-log reader uses the same shape. ",[214,1070,1071],{},"$host"," is the site or one of its ",[214,1074,596],{},[241,1076,1078],{"id":1077},"tasks","Tasks",[198,1080,1081,1082,349],{},"Long operations are tasks, stored as ",[214,1083,1084],{},"\u003Cbench>\u002Ftasks\u002F\u003CYYYYMMDD-HHMMSS-hex>\u002F",[930,1086,1087,1118],{},[933,1088,1089,1092,1093,615,1096,615,1099,615,1102,615,1105,615,1108,1111,1112,615,1115,225],{},[214,1090,1091],{},"meta.json",": ",[214,1094,1095],{},"task_id",[214,1097,1098],{},"command",[214,1100,1101],{},"args",[214,1103,1104],{},"queued_at",[214,1106,1107],{},"started_at",[214,1109,1110],{},"finished_at"," (UTC ISO-8601), ",[214,1113,1114],{},"exit_code",[214,1116,1117],{},"failure",[933,1119,1120,1092,1122,615,1125,615,1128,615,1131,502,1134,225],{},[214,1121,1045],{},[214,1123,1124],{},"queued",[214,1126,1127],{},"running",[214,1129,1130],{},"success",[214,1132,1133],{},"failed",[214,1135,1136],{},"killed",[198,1138,1139,1140,1143],{},"The directories are created with mode ",[214,1141,1142],{},"0700",", so only the bench user can read them.",[227,1145,1147],{"id":1146},"deployment-events-from-pilot-tasks","Deployment events from Pilot tasks",[198,1149,1150],{},"Wolf reports these task commands:",[198,1152,1153,615,1156,615,1159,615,1162,615,1165,615,1168,615,1171,615,1174,615,1177,615,1180,615,1183,615,1186,615,1189,615,1192,615,1195,615,1198,615,1201,615,1204,225],{},[214,1154,1155],{},"update",[214,1157,1158],{},"retry-update",[214,1160,1161],{},"complete-migration",[214,1163,1164],{},"migrate",[214,1166,1167],{},"revert-migration",[214,1169,1170],{},"revert-apps",[214,1172,1173],{},"revert-site",[214,1175,1176],{},"switch-branch",[214,1178,1179],{},"get-and-install-app",[214,1181,1182],{},"install-app",[214,1184,1185],{},"uninstall-app",[214,1187,1188],{},"remove-app",[214,1190,1191],{},"build",[214,1193,1194],{},"restart-services",[214,1196,1197],{},"switch-lite-mode",[214,1199,1200],{},"setup-nginx",[214,1202,1203],{},"restore-site",[214,1205,1206],{},"reinstall-site",[198,1208,1209,1210,217,1213,1216],{},"The site comes from the task's ",[214,1211,1212],{},"site",[214,1214,1215],{},"sites"," arguments. The bench is the Pilot bench itself, since tasks are per bench.",[241,1218,1220],{"id":1219},"where-tasks-are-read","Where tasks are read",[198,1222,1223],{},"Wolf tries two sources, in this order.",[1225,1226,1227,1272],"ol",{},[933,1228,1229,1092,1232,1235,1236,1239,1240,1243,1244,1247,1248,1251,1252,1254,1255,1258,1259,1261,1262,1264,1265,1267,1268,1271],{},[209,1230,1231],{},"Admin API",[214,1233,1234],{},"GET http:\u002F\u002F127.0.0.1:\u003Cadmin.port+1>\u002Fapi\u002Fv1\u002Ftasks?limit=100",". It returns ",[214,1237,1238],{},"TaskInfo.as_dict()"," rows. The endpoint needs a ",[209,1241,1242],{},"bench-scoped"," session: ",[214,1245,1246],{},"Authorization: Bearer \u003CJWT>",". Pilot signs these tokens locally with HS256 over ",[214,1249,1250],{},"{\"sub\": \"admin\", \"iat\", \"exp\", \"scope\": \"bench\", \"jti\"}"," using ",[214,1253,496],{},", and verifies them with ",[214,1256,1257],{},"require: [\"exp\"]",". Wolf uses ",[214,1260,484],{}," when you set one. Otherwise it mints a one-hour token with the same claim shape, from ",[214,1263,490],{}," or from ",[214,1266,254],{}," when Wolf can read it. Each minted token has a ",[214,1269,1270],{},"wolf-…"," jti, so it appears in Pilot's active sessions and can be revoked.",[933,1273,1274,1092,1277,259,1280,1282,1283,1285],{},[209,1275,1276],{},"Task files",[214,1278,1279],{},"\u003Cbench>\u002Ftasks\u002F*\u002Fmeta.json",[214,1281,1045],{},". This only works when the Wolf Agent runs as the bench user, because of the ",[214,1284,1142],{}," mode.",[241,1287,1289],{"id":1288},"how-events-are-produced","How events are produced",[198,1291,1292,1293,225],{},"Both sources follow the same rules as on ",[201,1294,45],{"href":46},[930,1296,1297,1308,1325,1331],{},[933,1298,713,1299,1301,1302,1304,1305,225],{},[214,1300,716],{}," event is sent when the task starts, timestamped at ",[214,1303,1107],{},". An incident during a long migrate links to it, for example through the \"502 spike after deployment\" ",[201,1306,1307],{"href":102},"preset",[933,1309,1310,1311,1313,1314,1316,1317,615,1320,259,1323,225],{},"An ",[214,1312,727],{}," event is sent if the task ends ",[214,1315,1133],{},". It carries ",[214,1318,1319],{},"failure.code",[214,1321,1322],{},"failure.message",[214,1324,1114],{},[933,1326,1327,1328,225],{},"Reported task ids are kept for 3 days in ",[214,1329,1330],{},"\u003Cspool_dir>\u002Fpilot-tasks.json",[933,1332,1333],{},"The first poll skips history and only picks up queued or running tasks.",[198,1335,1336,1337,1340,1341,225],{},"This replaces manual ",[214,1338,1339],{},"wolf-agent mark-deployment --source pilot"," markers on Pilot benches. Event fields are described in the ",[201,1342,1343],{"href":169},"protocol",[227,1345,1347],{"id":1346},"wolf-next-to-pilots-own-monitoring","Wolf next to Pilot's own monitoring",[198,1349,1350],{},"From the Pilot docs:",[930,1352,1353,1362,1372],{},[933,1354,1355,1358,1359,225],{},[214,1356,1357],{},"pilot-monitor.service"," collects host, database and bench metrics every 10 s and pings production sites every 5 s. Its logs go to ",[214,1360,1361],{},"system\u002Flogs\u002F",[933,1363,1364,1367,1368,1371],{},[214,1365,1366],{},"[resource_limits]"," raises CPU, memory, disk and uptime alerts after 5 minutes. They go to Central (on Central-managed hosts), to ",[214,1369,1370],{},"webhook_endpoints"," (POST with a Bearer header) and to mail.",[933,1373,1374,1377,1378,1381],{},[214,1375,1376],{},"[telemetry]"," ships metrics and logs (Fluent Bit tails ",[214,1379,1380],{},"benches\u002F*\u002Flogs\u002F*.log",") to a region's \"Datum\" endpoint with a Central-issued token.",[198,1383,1384],{},"Wolf reads the same local files and does not interfere with any of these. What it adds on a self-hosted Pilot host:",[930,1386,1387,1390,1393,1396],{},[933,1388,1389],{},"Tracebacks, failed scheduled jobs and worker crashes as events.",[933,1391,1392],{},"5xx\u002F502 per site.",[933,1394,1395],{},"SSH signals.",[933,1397,1398],{},"Incidents tied to the Pilot task that preceded them.",[198,1400,1401],{},"All of it is kept on your own Wolf site.",[1403,1404,1405],"note",{},[198,1406,1407,1408,1410],{},"Pilot's resource alerts could be pointed at Wolf through ",[214,1409,1370],{},", but their payload is not documented, so Wolf does not accept them yet.",[227,1412,1414],{"id":1413},"limitations-and-unverified-points","Limitations and unverified points",[241,1416,1418],{"id":1417},"what-pilot-would-need","What Pilot would need",[198,1420,1421],{},"These items from issue #17 need changes or answers from the Pilot maintainers:",[1225,1423,1424,1444,1460,1469],{},[933,1425,1426,1429,1430,1433,1434,1436,1437,615,1440,1443],{},[209,1427,1428],{},"\"Enable Wolf for this bench\" toggle."," A ",[214,1431,1432],{},"[wolf]"," table in ",[214,1435,254],{}," (",[214,1438,1439],{},"enabled",[214,1441,1442],{},"url",") plus an Admin settings switch, which would install and register the agent with the bench's paths. It belongs in frappe\u002Fpilot, and nothing like it exists there today.",[933,1445,1446,1449,1450,1452,1453,1456,1457,1459],{},[209,1447,1448],{},"A machine token for the Admin API."," Today a bench-scoped session is a 24 h password session, or a JWT signed with ",[214,1451,433],{}," or issued by the configured JWKS. A long-lived, read-only ",[214,1454,1455],{},"tasks:read"," token would avoid sharing ",[214,1458,433],{}," with Wolf.",[933,1461,1462,1465,1466,225],{},[209,1463,1464],{},"A task event feed"," (webhook or SSE across tasks) instead of polling ",[214,1467,1468],{},"\u002Ftasks",[933,1470,1471,1474,1475,259,1477,1479,1480,1482],{},[209,1472,1473],{},"File modes."," Confirmation that ",[214,1476,254],{},[214,1478,806],{}," stay readable for a monitoring group, since tasks are ",[214,1481,1142],{}," by design.",[241,1484,1485],{"id":705},"Unverified",[198,1487,1488],{},"These points come from reading the sources and running unit tests against fixtures built from them. Nothing has been run against a live Pilot host. In particular, these are untested:",[930,1490,1491,1494,1500,1505,1508],{},[933,1492,1493],{},"The minted token against a real Admin backend.",[933,1495,1496,1499],{},[214,1497,1498],{},"\u002Fapi\u002Fv1\u002Ftasks"," through Pilot's rate limits.",[933,1501,1502,1503,225],{},"File permissions for a non-bench user, including Pilot's modes for ",[214,1504,254],{},[933,1506,1507],{},"The exact worker queue-slug spelling on a running bench.",[933,1509,1510],{},"Pilot's exact systemd unit and supervisor program names, which process checks depend on.",[1512,1513,1514,1540,1545,1557,1562,1592,1596,1650,1654,1684,1688,1710,1714,1761,1765,1812,1817],"collapsible",{},[198,1515,1516,1517,1524,1525,1532,1533,225],{},"Everything on this page is read from frappe\u002Fpilot at commit ",[201,1518,1521],{"href":1519,"rel":1520},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Ffrappe\u002Fpilot\u002Ftree\u002F34613eade8008a15a9ae61d28fca2627db52e7b9",[205],[214,1522,1523],{},"34613ea"," (2026-10-29). Every link is pinned to it. The full write-up is ",[201,1526,1529],{"href":1527,"rel":1528},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fbthuner\u002Fdodock-wolf\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fdocs\u002Fpilot.md",[205],[214,1530,1531],{},"docs\u002Fpilot.md","; the Wolf side is ",[201,1534,1537],{"href":1535,"rel":1536},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fbthuner\u002Fdodock-wolf\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002Fagent\u002Fwolf_agent\u002Fpilot.py",[205],[214,1538,1539],{},"agent\u002Fwolf_